injectable tracer. And the computer

1114
00:41:13,599 --> 00:41:17,680
terminal ensures that everything runs

1115
00:41:15,280 --> 00:41:19,680
safely and precisely.

1116
00:41:17,680 --> 00:41:21,839
Together, these components allow us to

1117
00:41:19,680 --> 00:41:26,119
produce short-lived traces on demand for

1118
00:41:21,839 --> 00:41:26,119
clinical use in nuclear imaging.

1119
00:41:27,520 --> 00:41:30,800
The fourth method of producing

1120
00:41:28,880 --> 00:41:32,960
radionuclides and the one most relevant

1121
00:41:30,800 --> 00:41:35,599
to clinical imaging today is the use of

1122
00:41:32,960 --> 00:41:37,200
radionuclide generators.

1123
00:41:35,599 --> 00:41:40,480
A very well-known example is the

1124
00:41:37,200 --> 00:41:42,640
technium 99m generator. This system is

1125
00:41:40,480 --> 00:41:44,560
sometimes nicknamed the moly cow because

1126
00:41:42,640 --> 00:41:47,680
it is based on the parent isotope

1127
00:41:44,560 --> 00:41:50,560
malibdinum 99 which naturally decays to

1128
00:41:47,680 --> 00:41:52,880
technium 99m.

1129
00:41:50,560 --> 00:41:55,200
Just as a cow can be milked repeatedly,

1130
00:41:52,880 --> 00:41:58,000
the generator can be eluted or milked

1131
00:41:55,200 --> 00:41:59,839
each day to obtain fresh technium 99m

1132
00:41:58,000 --> 00:42:02,720
for imaging.

1133
00:41:59,839 --> 00:42:04,720
Technium 99M is especially important

1134
00:42:02,720 --> 00:42:07,200
because it is the most widely used

1135
00:42:04,720 --> 00:42:10,640
radionuclide in single photon emission

1136
00:42:07,200 --> 00:42:12,240
computed tomography or spec.

1137
00:42:10,640 --> 00:42:14,400
It provides the right balance of

1138
00:42:12,240 --> 00:42:17,359
half-life about 6 hours and gammaray

1139
00:42:14,400 --> 00:42:19,359
energy about 140 kilo electron volts

1140
00:42:17,359 --> 00:42:21,040
making it very effective for diagnostic

1141
00:42:19,359 --> 00:42:22,800
imaging while keeping the patient dose

1142
00:42:21,040 --> 00:42:24,400
reasonable.

1143
00:42:22,800 --> 00:42:26,319
This approach is extremely cost

1144
00:42:24,400 --> 00:42:28,640
effective compared to building a nuclear

1145
00:42:26,319 --> 00:42:30,319
reactor or cyclron. That is why

1146
00:42:28,640 --> 00:42:32,240
radionucline generators remain a

1147
00:42:30,319 --> 00:42:35,240
backbone of nuclear medicine practice

1148
00:42:32,240 --> 00:42:35,240
worldwide.

1149
00:42:36,880 --> 00:42:40,960
Let us now look more carefully at how

1150
00:42:38,400 --> 00:42:42,800
the technium generator actually works.

1151
00:42:40,960 --> 00:42:44,480
This system operates through a two-step

1152
00:42:42,800 --> 00:42:47,200
process.

1153
00:42:44,480 --> 00:42:48,800
The parent isotope is malibdinum 99

1154
00:42:47,200 --> 00:42:51,119
which is prepared and loaded into an

1155
00:42:48,800 --> 00:42:52,800
aluminina column inside the generator.

1156
00:42:51,119 --> 00:42:55,440
This column is shielded with lead for

1157
00:42:52,800 --> 00:42:57,839
safety. Over time, malibdinum 99

1158
00:42:55,440 --> 00:43:00,000
naturally decays to technium 99M, the

1159
00:42:57,839 --> 00:43:02,880
daughter isotope.

1160
00:43:00,000 --> 00:43:05,119
Technium 99M, however, binds only weakly

1161
00:43:02,880 --> 00:43:06,960
to the aluminina column. That means if

1162
00:43:05,119 --> 00:43:09,920
we pass a saline solution through the

1163
00:43:06,960 --> 00:43:12,480
column, it will wash the technium 99M

1164
00:43:09,920 --> 00:43:14,960
out while leaving the malibdinum 99

1165
00:43:12,480 --> 00:43:16,800
behind. This daily washing process is

1166
00:43:14,960 --> 00:43:19,119
often called milking the generator, just

1167
00:43:16,800 --> 00:43:21,760
like milking a cow. Each solution

1168
00:43:19,119 --> 00:43:23,920
provides a fresh supply of technium 99M

1169
00:43:21,760 --> 00:43:26,400
for clinical use.

1170
00:43:23,920 --> 00:43:28,800
Once obtained, the technium 99M is

1171
00:43:26,400 --> 00:43:30,720
injected into the patient's body. Inside

1172
00:43:28,800 --> 00:43:33,359
the body, it underos further decay to

1173
00:43:30,720 --> 00:43:35,119
technium 99, a stable isotope.

1174
00:43:33,359 --> 00:43:37,040
Importantly, this decay is accompanied

1175
00:43:35,119 --> 00:43:39,119
by the emission of gamma photons, which

1176
00:43:37,040 --> 00:43:41,440
can then be detected by imaging devices

1177
00:43:39,119 --> 00:43:43,200
such as a gamma camera.

1178
00:43:41,440 --> 00:43:45,200
From a modeling perspective, this is a

1179
00:43:43,200 --> 00:43:47,440
two-step decay chain. The parent

1180
00:43:45,200 --> 00:43:50,800
malibdinum 99 decays with its own

1181
00:43:47,440 --> 00:43:53,520
half-life to produce technium 99m. Then

1182
00:43:50,800 --> 00:43:55,920
technium 99m decays with a shorter

1183
00:43:53,520 --> 00:43:57,520
half-life into stable technium 99

1184
00:43:55,920 --> 00:43:59,280
releasing gamma radiation in the

1185
00:43:57,520 --> 00:44:00,800
process.

1186
00:43:59,280 --> 00:44:02,800
Each of these steps follows an

1187
00:44:00,800 --> 00:44:04,720
exponential law and when combined they

1188
00:44:02,800 --> 00:44:06,640
produce a dynamic interplay between

1189
00:44:04,720 --> 00:44:08,400
parent daughter and final stable

1190
00:44:06,640 --> 00:44:10,400
product.

1191
00:44:08,400 --> 00:44:12,640
This two-step process is what makes the

1192
00:44:10,400 --> 00:44:14,079
technium generator so effective. It

1193
00:44:12,640 --> 00:44:16,000
provides a steady supply of a

1194
00:44:14,079 --> 00:44:21,160
short-lived imaging isotope without

1195
00:44:16,000 --> 00:44:21,160
requiring a reactor or cyclron on site.

1196
00:44:22,560 --> 00:44:26,880
Now let us connect the generator process

1197
00:44:24,640 --> 00:44:28,480
to mathematical modeling. To properly

1198
00:44:26,880 --> 00:44:31,359
describe the production and decay of

1199
00:44:28,480 --> 00:44:33,760
technium 99m, we need three first order

1200
00:44:31,359 --> 00:44:36,800
differential equations. These equations

1201
00:44:33,760 --> 00:44:39,440
track the parent isotope malibdinum 99,

1202
00:44:36,800 --> 00:44:41,040
the daughter isotope technium 99m and

1203
00:44:39,440 --> 00:44:43,520
finally the stable granddaughter

1204
00:44:41,040 --> 00:44:46,000
technium 99.

1205
00:44:43,520 --> 00:44:48,079
The first equation describes the parent.

1206
00:44:46,000 --> 00:44:50,560
It decays exponentially at a constant

1207
00:44:48,079 --> 00:44:52,640
rate. As we already studied, the second

1208
00:44:50,560 --> 00:44:54,800
equation describes the daughter technium

1209
00:44:52,640 --> 00:44:56,319
99m.

1210
00:44:54,800 --> 00:44:58,800
This one is more interesting because it

1211
00:44:56,319 --> 00:45:00,640
has two contributions. One positive term

1212
00:44:58,800 --> 00:45:02,160
which comes from the decay of the parent

1213
00:45:00,640 --> 00:45:03,920
feeding into the daughter and one

1214
00:45:02,160 --> 00:45:06,640
negative term which accounts for the

1215
00:45:03,920 --> 00:45:08,000
daughter decaying further. Finally, the

1216
00:45:06,640 --> 00:45:10,079
third equation describes the

1217
00:45:08,000 --> 00:45:12,000
granddaughter which only has a positive

1218
00:45:10,079 --> 00:45:13,839
contribution coming from the decay of

1219
00:45:12,000 --> 00:45:16,079
the daughter.

1220
00:45:13,839 --> 00:45:18,000
If you look closely, you will see that

1221
00:45:16,079 --> 00:45:20,240
the daughter equation is not purely

1222
00:45:18,000 --> 00:45:22,800
exponential. It is influenced by both

1223
00:45:20,240 --> 00:45:24,640
the parent and its own decay. To solve

1224
00:45:22,800 --> 00:45:26,319
this type of system, we use standard

1225
00:45:24,640 --> 00:45:28,400
methods for ordinary differential

1226
00:45:26,319 --> 00:45:30,319
equations.

1227
00:45:28,400 --> 00:45:32,160
Specifically, the daughter solution is

1228
00:45:30,319 --> 00:45:34,319
expressed as the sum of two parts. A

1229
00:45:32,160 --> 00:45:36,400
homogeneous solution which describes the

1230
00:45:34,319 --> 00:45:38,079
natural decay and a particular solution

1231
00:45:36,400 --> 00:45:40,560
which accounts for the contribution from

1232
00:45:38,079 --> 00:45:43,359
the parent. These two components combine

1233
00:45:40,560 --> 00:45:45,200
to give the real physical solution.

1234
00:45:43,359 --> 00:45:47,280
The important point here is not to get

1235
00:45:45,200 --> 00:45:49,440
lost in the algebra but to recognize the

1236
00:45:47,280 --> 00:45:51,440
principle. Exponential decay chains can

1237
00:45:49,440 --> 00:45:53,359
be modeled systematically and by solving

1238
00:45:51,440 --> 00:45:56,160
these equations we can predict the time

1239
00:45:53,359 --> 00:45:58,880
course of technium 99er production and

1240
00:45:56,160 --> 00:46:00,720
availability in a generator.

1241
00:45:58,880 --> 00:46:02,319
This is crucial in practice because it

1242
00:46:00,720 --> 00:46:04,160
tells us how much tracer will be

1243
00:46:02,319 --> 00:46:08,599
available at a given time and when to

1244
00:46:04,160 --> 00:46:08,599
perform illusion for maximum yield.

1245
00:46:10,000 --> 00:46:14,960
Now let's make sense of the daily yield

1246
00:46:11,920 --> 00:46:16,960
from a radionuclide generator.

1247
00:46:14,960 --> 00:46:19,839
On the left graph, the dashed line shows

1248
00:46:16,960 --> 00:46:22,560
the parent isotope malibdum 99 which

1249
00:46:19,839 --> 00:46:25,680
slowly decays over time. The solid line

1250
00:46:22,560 --> 00:46:27,520
shows the daughter isotope technium 99m

1251
00:46:25,680 --> 00:46:29,520
which gradually builds up as the parent

1252
00:46:27,520 --> 00:46:31,599
decays. At first the daughter

1253
00:46:29,520 --> 00:46:35,760
accumulates rapidly but eventually a

1254
00:46:31,599 --> 00:46:37,520
balance is reached. Why?

1255
00:46:35,760 --> 00:46:39,280
Because as more daughter atoms appear,

1256
00:46:37,520 --> 00:46:41,280
they also begin to decay at a faster

1257
00:46:39,280 --> 00:46:43,119
rate. At some point, the rate of

1258
00:46:41,280 --> 00:46:45,280
production from the parent equals the

1259
00:46:43,119 --> 00:46:47,280
rate of decay of the daughter. That

1260
00:46:45,280 --> 00:46:49,119
balance defines the maximum activity of

1261
00:46:47,280 --> 00:46:50,880
the daughter.

1262
00:46:49,119 --> 00:46:52,800
This is the key point emphasized in the

1263
00:46:50,880 --> 00:46:54,560
text. The effective decay rate of the

1264
00:46:52,800 --> 00:46:56,640
daughter is governed not by its own

1265
00:46:54,560 --> 00:46:58,960
half-life alone, but by the half-life of

1266
00:46:56,640 --> 00:47:00,800
the parent. The system naturally seeks

1267
00:46:58,960 --> 00:47:03,760
equilibrium. So, the ratio between

1268
00:47:00,800 --> 00:47:05,200
parent and daughter becomes constant.

1269
00:47:03,760 --> 00:47:07,760
On the right hand graph you see the

1270
00:47:05,200 --> 00:47:09,680
practical outcome. Each spike represents

1271
00:47:07,760 --> 00:47:11,280
an illusion where the daughter isotope

1272
00:47:09,680 --> 00:47:13,440
is washed out of the generator for

1273
00:47:11,280 --> 00:47:15,440
clinical use.

1274
00:47:13,440 --> 00:47:18,000
Typically this is done once every 24

1275
00:47:15,440 --> 00:47:19,760
hours. After each illusion the daughter

1276
00:47:18,000 --> 00:47:22,160
begins to build up again from the parent

1277
00:47:19,760 --> 00:47:24,640
forming another peak. Over the course of

1278
00:47:22,160 --> 00:47:26,480
days however the overall yield decreases

1279
00:47:24,640 --> 00:47:28,480
because the parent itself is decaying

1280
00:47:26,480 --> 00:47:30,400
exponentially.

1281
00:47:28,480 --> 00:47:32,400
So in practice you get this repeating

1282
00:47:30,400 --> 00:47:34,560
cycle. Each day you harvest a certain

1283
00:47:32,400 --> 00:47:36,720
amount of technium 99m, use it for

1284
00:47:34,560 --> 00:47:38,720
imaging and then allow the generator to

1285
00:47:36,720 --> 00:47:40,400
recharge.

1286
00:47:38,720 --> 00:47:42,319
After about a week, the parent has

1287
00:47:40,400 --> 00:47:44,079
decayed so much that the yield becomes

1288
00:47:42,319 --> 00:47:45,920
too low and the generator must be

1289
00:47:44,079 --> 00:47:47,520
replaced.

1290
00:47:45,920 --> 00:47:50,240
This is the essence of milking a

1291
00:47:47,520 --> 00:47:52,160
radionuclide generator. An elegant and

1292
00:47:50,240 --> 00:47:54,319
cost-effective way to provide a steady

1293
00:47:52,160 --> 00:47:57,319
supply of short-lived traces for nuclear

1294
00:47:54,319 --> 00:47:57,319
medicine.

1295
00:47:58,800 --> 00:48:03,760
Now let's look at how technium 99m is

1296
00:48:01,520 --> 00:48:04,960
actually used in medicine. This table

1297
00:48:03,760 --> 00:48:06,800
lists some of the most common

1298
00:48:04,960 --> 00:48:08,560
radioarmaceuticals and their clinical

1299
00:48:06,800 --> 00:48:10,079
applications. What you can see

1300
00:48:08,560 --> 00:48:12,400
immediately is how versatile this

1301
00:48:10,079 --> 00:48:14,880
isotope is. It can target almost every

1302
00:48:12,400 --> 00:48:16,720
major system of the body.

1303
00:48:14,880 --> 00:48:18,720
For example, technium labeled

1304
00:48:16,720 --> 00:48:20,800
macroaggregated albamin is used for

1305
00:48:18,720 --> 00:48:22,880
pulmonary perfusion studies helping us

1306
00:48:20,800 --> 00:48:25,040
assess blood flow in the lungs.

1307
00:48:22,880 --> 00:48:26,800
Difhosphinates labeled with technium are

1308
00:48:25,040 --> 00:48:28,240
widely applied in skeletal imaging

1309
00:48:26,800 --> 00:48:30,319
especially for detecting bone

1310
00:48:28,240 --> 00:48:31,680
metastases.

1311
00:48:30,319 --> 00:48:34,160
For the brain, compounds like

1312
00:48:31,680 --> 00:48:37,040
glucaeptinate or hmpo can be used to

1313
00:48:34,160 --> 00:48:39,200
image tumors or measure brain perusion.

1314
00:48:37,040 --> 00:48:41,200
Sulfur colloid labeled with technium

1315
00:48:39,200 --> 00:48:44,160
allows us to visualize the liver, spleen

1316
00:48:41,200 --> 00:48:46,400
and even sentininal lymph nodes.

1317
00:48:44,160 --> 00:48:48,480
DTPA is useful for renal function and

1318
00:48:46,400 --> 00:48:50,480
pulmonary ventilation studies and

1319
00:48:48,480 --> 00:48:52,800
compounds like cesme are used to

1320
00:48:50,480 --> 00:48:54,960
evaluate mioardial profusion making

1321
00:48:52,800 --> 00:48:57,040
technium imaging an essential tool in

1322
00:48:54,960 --> 00:48:59,680
cardiology.

1323
00:48:57,040 --> 00:49:03,280
So what do we learn from this?

1324
00:48:59,680 --> 00:49:05,359
With just a single isotope technium 99m

1325
00:49:03,280 --> 00:49:07,359
we can design radioarmaceuticals to

1326
00:49:05,359 --> 00:49:09,599
study the lungs, bones, brain, liver,

1327
00:49:07,359 --> 00:49:12,240
kidneys, heart and more. This is one of

1328
00:49:09,599 --> 00:49:14,960
the main reasons technium 99m became the

1329
00:49:12,240 --> 00:49:16,640
workhorse of nuclear medicine.

1330
00:49:14,960 --> 00:49:18,720
With that we finish our discussion of

1331
00:49:16,640 --> 00:49:20,960
tracer production. We have seen the

1332
00:49:18,720 --> 00:49:22,319
different ways isotopes can be generated

1333
00:49:20,960 --> 00:49:24,559
particularly the third and fourth

1334
00:49:22,319 --> 00:49:26,240
methods. Cyclrons for producing positron

1335
00:49:24,559 --> 00:49:28,880
emitters used in PET imaging and

1336
00:49:26,240 --> 00:49:31,280
generators for producing technium 99m

1337
00:49:28,880 --> 00:49:32,800
used in spec imaging.

1338
00:49:31,280 --> 00:49:35,119
Now we move into the last part of

1339
00:49:32,800 --> 00:49:37,599
today's lecture data acquisition. Here

1340
00:49:35,119 --> 00:49:39,920
we'll focus on two main approaches. The

1341
00:49:37,599 --> 00:49:42,160
first is the gamma camera which detects

1342
00:49:39,920 --> 00:49:44,400
single gamma ray photons and is central

1343
00:49:42,160 --> 00:49:46,880
to spec or single photon emission

1344
00:49:44,400 --> 00:49:48,960
computed tomography.

1345
00:49:46,880 --> 00:49:50,960
The second is coincidence detection

1346
00:49:48,960 --> 00:49:53,200
which captures pairs of gamma photons

1347
00:49:50,960 --> 00:49:55,440
emitted simultaneously and this is the

1348
00:49:53,200 --> 00:49:57,280
basis of pet or posetron emission

1349
00:49:55,440 --> 00:49:59,119
tomography.

1350
00:49:57,280 --> 00:50:01,200
As we go through this, keep in mind the

1351
00:49:59,119 --> 00:50:03,200
difference. SPECT relies on detecting

1352
00:50:01,200 --> 00:50:05,119
individual gamma photons while PET

1353
00:50:03,200 --> 00:50:07,359
relies on detecting photon pairs from

1354
00:50:05,119 --> 00:50:09,200
posetron annihilation. And this

1355
00:50:07,359 --> 00:50:13,400
difference has profound implications for

1356
00:50:09,200 --> 00:50:13,400
scanner design and image quality.

1357
00:50:14,800 --> 00:50:18,640
So that concludes the third part where

1358
00:50:16,640 --> 00:50:20,640
we discussed radioactivity and tracer

1359
00:50:18,640 --> 00:50:22,960
production. We learned about the four

1360
00:50:20,640 --> 00:50:24,640
methods of producing radionuclides with

1361
00:50:22,960 --> 00:50:27,200
special focus on the third and fourth

1362
00:50:24,640 --> 00:50:29,359
methods. Cyclrons for posetron emission

1363
00:50:27,200 --> 00:50:31,680
tomography and radionuclide generators

1364
00:50:29,359 --> 00:50:33,200
for single photon emission tomography.

1365
00:50:31,680 --> 00:50:35,920
Together these methods provide the

1366
00:50:33,200 --> 00:50:37,760
backbone of nuclear medicine.

1367
00:50:35,920 --> 00:50:40,319
Now let's move on to the final part of

1368
00:50:37,760 --> 00:50:41,920
today's lecture. Data acquisition. This

1369
00:50:40,319 --> 00:50:44,160
is where the signals generated by

1370
00:50:41,920 --> 00:50:47,040
radioactive decay are actually detected

1371
00:50:44,160 --> 00:50:48,800
and transformed into images.

1372
00:50:47,040 --> 00:50:50,880
There are two main approaches we need to

1373
00:50:48,800 --> 00:50:52,800
understand. The first is the gamma

1374
00:50:50,880 --> 00:50:55,359
camera which is used in single photon

1375
00:50:52,800 --> 00:50:57,119
emission computed tomography or spec.

1376
00:50:55,359 --> 00:51:00,240
The gamma camera captures individual

1377
00:50:57,119 --> 00:51:02,160
gammaray photons one by one.

1378
00:51:00,240 --> 00:51:03,920
The second approach is coincidence

1379
00:51:02,160 --> 00:51:06,640
detection which is the principle behind

1380
00:51:03,920 --> 00:51:08,640
posetron emission tomography or PET. In

1381
00:51:06,640 --> 00:51:10,720
this case, we don't just detect single

1382
00:51:08,640 --> 00:51:13,119
photons. Instead, we detect pairs of

1383
00:51:10,720 --> 00:51:16,079
photons that are emitted simultaneously

1384
00:51:13,119 --> 00:51:18,160
traveling in opposite directions.

1385
00:51:16,079 --> 00:51:20,079
Why does this happen? Because when a

1386
00:51:18,160 --> 00:51:21,839
posetron encounters an electron, the two

1387
00:51:20,079 --> 00:51:23,680
annihilate, producing a pair of gamma

1388
00:51:21,839 --> 00:51:25,680
photons.

1389
00:51:23,680 --> 00:51:28,160
Detecting these pairs in coincidence

1390
00:51:25,680 --> 00:51:29,920
allows PET to provide highly accurate

1391
00:51:28,160 --> 00:51:33,119
information about the location of the

1392
00:51:29,920 --> 00:51:35,920
annihilation event inside the body.

1393
00:51:33,119 --> 00:51:38,400
So in summary, SPECT relies on detecting

1394
00:51:35,920 --> 00:51:40,640
single photons with a gamma camera while

1395
00:51:38,400 --> 00:51:42,960
PET relies on detecting photon pairs

1396
00:51:40,640 --> 00:51:44,880
through coincidence detection. This

1397
00:51:42,960 --> 00:51:46,559
distinction has a profound effect on how

1398
00:51:44,880 --> 00:51:50,520
scanners are designed and on the quality

1399
00:51:46,559 --> 00:51:50,520
of the images they produce.

1400
00:51:52,160 --> 00:51:55,520
Now let's look more carefully at the

1401
00:51:53,680 --> 00:51:57,280
principle of the gamma camera which is

1402
00:51:55,520 --> 00:51:59,680
one of the most important devices in

1403
00:51:57,280 --> 00:52:01,680
nuclear medicine imaging. I've placed a

1404
00:51:59,680 --> 00:52:04,079
red diamond here to highlight that this

1405
00:52:01,680 --> 00:52:05,839
concept is essential.

1406
00:52:04,079 --> 00:52:08,720
The very first step in the system is the

1407
00:52:05,839 --> 00:52:10,160
columator. Without columnation, gamma

1408
00:52:08,720 --> 00:52:11,839
photons would be arriving at the

1409
00:52:10,160 --> 00:52:13,680
detector from all directions and we

1410
00:52:11,839 --> 00:52:15,920
wouldn't know where they came from. The

1411
00:52:13,680 --> 00:52:17,680
columator, usually made of heavy metal,

1412
00:52:15,920 --> 00:52:19,359
such as lead, only allows photons

1413
00:52:17,680 --> 00:52:21,280
traveling along certain directions to

1414
00:52:19,359 --> 00:52:23,040
pass through.

1415
00:52:21,280 --> 00:52:25,760
In this way, we can establish the line

1416
00:52:23,040 --> 00:52:27,280
of response. Only photons traveling more

1417
00:52:25,760 --> 00:52:28,559
or less straight along the openings are

1418
00:52:27,280 --> 00:52:31,040
detected, while those coming from

1419
00:52:28,559 --> 00:52:32,800
oblique angles are blocked. This is very

1420
00:52:31,040 --> 00:52:34,480
similar in spirit to X-ray imaging where

1421
00:52:32,800 --> 00:52:37,839
each measurement corresponds to a line

1422
00:52:34,480 --> 00:52:39,520
integral along a particular direction.

1423
00:52:37,839 --> 00:52:41,920
The choice of columator is closely

1424
00:52:39,520 --> 00:52:43,839
linked to photon energy. If the gamma

1425
00:52:41,920 --> 00:52:45,760
rays have too low in energy, they will

1426
00:52:43,839 --> 00:52:48,000
be absorbed within the body and never

1427
00:52:45,760 --> 00:52:50,319
reach the detector.

1428
00:52:48,000 --> 00:52:52,400
If the energy is too high, the columator

1429
00:52:50,319 --> 00:52:55,280
cannot stop the oblique photon. So the

1430
00:52:52,400 --> 00:52:57,119
image contrast is lost. That is why for

1431
00:52:55,280 --> 00:53:00,240
clinical nuclear medicine we typically

1432
00:52:57,119 --> 00:53:02,319
work in the range of about 100 to 200 KV

1433
00:53:00,240 --> 00:53:05,200
a compromise between tissue penetration

1434
00:53:02,319 --> 00:53:07,440
and columator effectiveness.

1435
00:53:05,200 --> 00:53:09,839
Once a photon passes the columator it

1436
00:53:07,440 --> 00:53:12,160
strikes the scintillation crystal. This

1437
00:53:09,839 --> 00:53:14,160
crystal usually sodium iodide doped with

1438
00:53:12,160 --> 00:53:17,040
thallium emits a flash of visible light

1439
00:53:14,160 --> 00:53:18,880
when it absorbs a gamma photon.

1440
00:53:17,040 --> 00:53:21,280
That flash is extremely faint so it is

1441
00:53:18,880 --> 00:53:23,280
coupled to photo multiplier tubes. The

1442
00:53:21,280 --> 00:53:26,319
photo multipliers amplify the light

1443
00:53:23,280 --> 00:53:28,079
signal into an electrical pulse.

1444
00:53:26,319 --> 00:53:30,000
Then through a network, sometimes called

1445
00:53:28,079 --> 00:53:31,920
the anger logic or anger position

1446
00:53:30,000 --> 00:53:34,079
circuit, the system calculates the

1447
00:53:31,920 --> 00:53:35,680
location where the photon entered the

1448
00:53:34,079 --> 00:53:37,599
crystal.

1449
00:53:35,680 --> 00:53:39,760
A pulse height analyzer checks the

1450
00:53:37,599 --> 00:53:42,079
photon's energy, ensuring we only accept

1451
00:53:39,760 --> 00:53:43,839
photons in the desired energy window.

1452
00:53:42,079 --> 00:53:45,680
Finally, the computer records the

1453
00:53:43,839 --> 00:53:47,440
position and energy, gradually building

1454
00:53:45,680 --> 00:53:49,599
up an image of tracer distribution

1455
00:53:47,440 --> 00:53:52,240
inside the body.

1456
00:53:49,599 --> 00:53:53,920
So the key sequences columator to select

1457
00:53:52,240 --> 00:53:55,440
direction, scintillation crystal to

1458
00:53:53,920 --> 00:53:57,359
convert gamma to light, photo

1459
00:53:55,440 --> 00:53:59,119
multipliers to amplify the signal,

1460
00:53:57,359 --> 00:54:00,800
electronics to analyze energy and

1461
00:53:59,119 --> 00:54:04,440
position, and finally the computer to

1462
00:54:00,800 --> 00:54:04,440
assemble the image.

1463
00:54:05,839 --> 00:54:09,440
Now let's focus specifically on the

1464
00:54:07,680 --> 00:54:11,200
columator, which is really the heart of

1465
00:54:09,440 --> 00:54:13,119
how a gamma camera defines image

1466
00:54:11,200 --> 00:54:14,800
geometry.

1467
00:54:13,119 --> 00:54:16,480
What you see here on the left is the top

1468
00:54:14,800 --> 00:54:18,640
view of a typical parallel hole

1469
00:54:16,480 --> 00:54:20,240
columator. The structure is usually made

1470
00:54:18,640 --> 00:54:22,640
of lead with many closely packed

1471
00:54:20,240 --> 00:54:24,640
hexagonal holes.

1472
00:54:22,640 --> 00:54:26,640
Each hole acts like a channel allowing

1473
00:54:24,640 --> 00:54:27,920
only gamma photons traveling nearly

1474
00:54:26,640 --> 00:54:30,319
straight through to reach the

1475
00:54:27,920 --> 00:54:32,000
scintillation crystal behind it. On the

1476
00:54:30,319 --> 00:54:34,240
right, you see a side view. The holes

1477
00:54:32,000 --> 00:54:36,720
have length L, diameter D, and are

1478
00:54:34,240 --> 00:54:38,480
separated by scepter of thickness T.

1479
00:54:36,720 --> 00:54:41,520
These geometric parameters determine

1480
00:54:38,480 --> 00:54:43,839
both resolution and sensitivity.

1481
00:54:41,520 --> 00:54:45,760
Here's the trade-off. If the holes are

1482
00:54:43,839 --> 00:54:47,520
made very long and narrow, then photons

1483
00:54:45,760 --> 00:54:49,760
coming in at even a small angle will be

1484
00:54:47,520 --> 00:54:51,520
blocked. That means you achieve high

1485
00:54:49,760 --> 00:54:55,440
spatial resolution, you know much more

1486
00:54:51,520 --> 00:54:57,200
precisely where the photon came from.

1487
00:54:55,440 --> 00:54:59,280
But the price you pay is that most

1488
00:54:57,200 --> 00:55:01,200
photons are rejected. So the overall

1489
00:54:59,280 --> 00:55:03,359
sensitivity is low and the image is

1490
00:55:01,200 --> 00:55:05,359
noisy. On the other hand, if the holes

1491
00:55:03,359 --> 00:55:07,280
are short and wide, more photons get

1492
00:55:05,359 --> 00:55:10,079
through, improving sensitivity, but at

1493
00:55:07,280 --> 00:55:12,559
the cost of blurred resolution.

1494
00:55:10,079 --> 00:55:14,319
Another key factor is photon energy. For

1495
00:55:12,559 --> 00:55:16,640
nuclear medicine, we typically want

1496
00:55:14,319 --> 00:55:20,400
gammaray energies between about 100 and

1497
00:55:16,640 --> 00:55:21,920
200 KV. Below 100 kV, photons are

1498
00:55:20,400 --> 00:55:25,680
strongly absorbed in the body before

1499
00:55:21,920 --> 00:55:28,160
they even reach the detector.

1500
00:55:25,680 --> 00:55:29,839
Above 200 KV, the photons are so

1501
00:55:28,160 --> 00:55:31,920
energetic that they can penetrate

1502
00:55:29,839 --> 00:55:33,760
through the column receptor, creating

1503
00:55:31,920 --> 00:55:37,040
background counts and reducing image

1504
00:55:33,760 --> 00:55:39,920
contrast. That's why Technium 99M with

1505
00:55:37,040 --> 00:55:42,640
its 140 KV gamma emission is nearly

1506
00:55:39,920 --> 00:55:44,319
ideal for routine imaging.

1507
00:55:42,640 --> 00:55:46,400
And remember columators are not always

1508
00:55:44,319 --> 00:55:48,400
parallel hole. There are many other

1509
00:55:46,400 --> 00:55:50,720
designs. Pinhole columators for

1510
00:55:48,400 --> 00:55:52,720
magnification, fan beam columators for

1511
00:55:50,720 --> 00:55:54,559
brain and heart imaging and converging

1512
00:55:52,720 --> 00:55:56,880
or diverging types depending on the

1513
00:55:54,559 --> 00:55:58,720
clinical application.

1514
00:55:56,880 --> 00:56:00,880
Each design balances resolution and

1515
00:55:58,720 --> 00:56:03,119
sensitivity in a different way. So the

1516
00:56:00,880 --> 00:56:05,119
columator is not just a block of lead.

1517
00:56:03,119 --> 00:56:07,359
It is a carefully engineered component

1518
00:56:05,119 --> 00:56:10,359
that defines image quality in nuclear

1519
00:56:07,359 --> 00:56:10,359
medicine.

1520
00:56:11,920 --> 00:56:15,839
Now let's take a closer look at the

1521
00:56:13,599 --> 00:56:19,040
different columator designs and how each

1522
00:56:15,839 --> 00:56:20,480
one affects imaging performance.

1523
00:56:19,040 --> 00:56:22,400
Starting with the parallel hole

1524
00:56:20,480 --> 00:56:24,720
columator shown at the top left. This is

1525
00:56:22,400 --> 00:56:26,480
the most commonly used design. In this

1526
00:56:24,720 --> 00:56:29,119
case, the object and the image appear at

1527
00:56:26,480 --> 00:56:30,799
the same scale. It's simple, robust, and

1528
00:56:29,119 --> 00:56:32,880
widely applied in routine nuclear

1529
00:56:30,799 --> 00:56:34,319
medicine imaging.

1530
00:56:32,880 --> 00:56:37,040
Next, on the top right, we have the

1531
00:56:34,319 --> 00:56:39,119
diverging columator. Here, the holes fan

1532
00:56:37,040 --> 00:56:41,359
outward. The effect is that the image is

1533
00:56:39,119 --> 00:56:42,880
smaller than the object. This type is

1534
00:56:41,359 --> 00:56:44,720
