1550
00:57:15,359 --> 00:57:20,079
downside is that sensitivity is poor.

1551
00:57:17,520 --> 00:57:22,319
Most photons are blocked.

1552
00:57:20,079 --> 00:57:24,079
The key idea is always a trade-off. If

1553
00:57:22,319 --> 00:57:26,000
you make the holes or aperture smaller,

1554
00:57:24,079 --> 00:57:27,680
you gain higher spatial resolution, but

1555
00:57:26,000 --> 00:57:29,760
you lose sensitivity and the images

1556
00:57:27,680 --> 00:57:31,440
become noisier.

1557
00:57:29,760 --> 00:57:33,119
If you make them larger, you collect

1558
00:57:31,440 --> 00:57:36,000
more photons, but the resolution

1559
00:57:33,119 --> 00:57:37,440
decreases. Designing columnators is

1560
00:57:36,000 --> 00:57:39,760
therefore about finding the right

1561
00:57:37,440 --> 00:57:41,520
balance between resolution, sensitivity,

1562
00:57:39,760 --> 00:57:44,680
and the clinical question you are trying

1563
00:57:41,520 --> 00:57:44,680
